%% source: docs/statement.md §1 (claim and the R² evidence), §2 (three mechanisms), §3 (two policy moves), §4 (fairness); the limitation line is the scope boundary stated in docs/report.md ([Q25])
flowchart TD
  C["Claim: the attribution of academic outcomes must abandon single-minded meritocratic worship and face the constraint that family wealth and social background impose"]
  W1["Warrant 1: across 3,630 graduated and withdrawn students, wealth background carries the largest McFadden R² of the three layers, 0.2227"]
  W2["Warrant 2: ability adds only R² 0.05999, and parental cultural capital contributes 0.01572 on its own"]
  O["Condition: each layer has a statable mechanism (non-payment precedes withdrawal, the scholarship absorbs the shock, ability accumulates during study)"]
  P["Policy: payment status and funding eligibility rank first in the early-warning system; financial aid and academic support are delivered at the same point"]
  R["Conclusion: the underlying structure of academic outcomes is financial condition, so policy should centre on financial support"]
  N["Object of criticism: meritocratic worship, i.e. attributing academic outcomes directly to fixed ability"]
  X["Limitation: socio-economic background is recorded at a single point in time and the grounds for withdrawal are blank in the records, so causation rests on temporal precedence ([Q25])"]
  C --> W1
  W1 --> W2
  W2 --> O
  O --> P
  P --> R
  R --> N
  O -.-> X
  classDef open stroke-dasharray: 5 5,stroke:#b45309,color:#92400e,fill:#fffbeb
  class X open
